{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And ram skins.</b> That they are large, and this craft is in the land of Al-Gudmās, and it is called Gudmānsī." "<b>Tahashim.</b> It was a creature known in those days, for thus it is written, ואנעלך תחש (Ezekiel 16:10), and so it was already known." "<b>And shittim wood.</b> Some of our predecessors said that Jacob our father planted them, and Israel brought them out of Egypt by Moses' command, and the proof is וכל אשר נמצא אתו (below, 35:24), like the tekhelet and the argaman, and one may wonder why it says אשר נמצא אתו, for his needs, and if we say so, one may wonder why they brought out shittim wood, for what need did they have for them? Moreover, the Egyptians thought that they were going to slaughter and would then return, and therefore they lent to them, so how would they bring out many planks, each ten cubits long, and bars as well, and they passed over Egypt, the seat of kingship, and what answer would they give to those who asked: why are they taking shittim wood, when they are going to slaughter a three days' journey? Now we do not know whether there was a tradition in our fathers' hands that they brought them out of Egypt — if so, we will turn to their authority. But if it is mere reasoning, another path must be sought. And we say that near Mount Sinai there was a forest of shittim trees, and when they arrived there, he told them that they would remain there a long time, and the cloud was not upon them, as I have explained; so each one made a booth, and the princes made structures like courtyards, each according to his rank, and they cut down the entire forest, for they were a numerous people and made booths — and Moses said nothing to them about the Tabernacle until after the Day of Atonement. And this is the meaning of וכל אשר נמצא אתו."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:13.476755564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}